  partName: Fuel Pump
  description: The Fuel Pump is located at the top-left-front of the rocket engine
    and is made of a durable Pompe material, which provides a high level of resistance
    to corrosion and wear. This medium-sized, elongated component is responsible
    for pressurizing and delivering fuel to the combustion chamber, playing a critical
    role in the engine's overall performance and efficiency. Notably, the fuel pump
    is designed to operate at extremely high pressures and flow rates, making it
    a challenging component to design and manufacture.
